Well, I was quite sure I would have to explain on special levels history, so
here it is....

One year ago (at least) on early 3.0 development the team felt we should add
some 'atmosphere' levels. As I had implemented a castle level in 2.3 (never
posted through) I started to work on the level compiler (we didn't want the
level descriptions to be included in the code) with the castle/stronghold in
mind.
This is probably why it's, on my mind at least, the best sp_lev I designed.
About the tower, I wanted to have some place, inside Hell, to put the
dreadful Vlad (it was the stronger monster we had at that time :-). So
I had that tower idea : a 3 level tower that you can only enter (and exit
to answer previous msg) via it's bottommost level.
What I failed here is to give the player good reasons (rewards ?) to nuke
the b*stard. I did put some stuff here, but poly-pile trick make this
ridiculous...
However, I'm planning to enhance sp_levs for 3.1 and probably modify that
tower...

Hope this will clarify special levels look and feel (no copyright here :-).

